% global_cardinality with CONSTANT counts, under SEARCH (M7-T18, D-0082).
%
% M7-T16 refused a constant count; M7-T18 makes it the count VIEW [View.const k], whose
% counting row is the one-value variable's row with an empty ladder (see
% lib/core/prop/gcc.ml, "Constant counts"). Satisfiable, per D-0053, and built so the
% COUNTING derivation is on the page under a decision rather than settled at the root
% (the M7-T16 handoff's point about alldiff_hall_sat).
%
% It is test/unit/test_trace.ml's [ix10_gcc_source] with the counts written as the
% constants they always were (one 2, two 3s). p is confined to 2..3 by two linear rows
% and r, t by their sum, so {p, r, t} use up the cover's whole capacity over [2, 3] and
% rule A pushes q OUT of [2, 3] -- a sum ACROSS two cover values, and so a line that is
% not RUP against the .opb alone (I-X10). indomain_min tries q = 1 first; int_ne(q, 1)
% refutes it, the branch fails, and the capacity push's trace line goes on the page with
% its `pol` written ahead of it (M7-T17).
%
% MEASURED, and the reason this lane exists rather than a simpler one: make rule A's
% pushes WITHOUT [Store.deriving_ahead] and this proof is refused by 3.0.2 ("not implied
% by reverse unit propagation"); gcc_search_sat and gcc_const_counts_unsat still verify.
var 1..4: q :: output_var;
var 1..4: p :: output_var;
var 2..4: r :: output_var;
var 2..4: t :: output_var;
constraint int_lin_le([1],[p],3);
constraint int_lin_le([-1],[p],-2);
constraint int_lin_le([1,1],[r,t],5);
constraint fzn_global_cardinality([q,p,r,t],[2,3],[1,2]);
constraint int_ne(q,1);
solve :: int_search([q,p,r,t], input_order, indomain_min, complete) satisfy;
